  "body": "Related to #93.\r\nSteps 5 and 6 in the algorithm are\r\n```\r\n5. Let index be 0. \r\n6. Let parsed number be sequence[index] & ~mask. \r\n```\r\nThis seems like a mistake, since the first four bytes of `sequence` have already been compared to static values at the beginning of the [`matches the signature for WebM`](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#matches-the-signature-for-webm) algorithm (which is the only caller of [`parse a vint`](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-a-vint)) and therefore can't contain data that we would need to parse.\r\n\r\nWould I be correct in assuming that `index` should initially be equal to `iter` instead?",
